[h1]Recurring Diplomacy by Najane[/h1]

Diplomatic agreements in Civilization VII run out - Open Borders, Research Collaboration, Counterspy and the rest last a set number of turns, and then you have to remember to propose them again. And when you are short of Influence, you have to keep checking back until you can afford what you wanted. This mod does both for you.

[b]No rules change.[/b] Every proposal it sends is one you could make yourself from the Diplomacy screen, at the same Influence price, and the other leader can still say no.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Two buttons beside every price[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Sync - keep it running.[/b] Switch it on beside any treaty, endeavour, espionage action or sanction on a leader's Diplomacy screen, and the action is started now if possible, then proposed again at the start of your turn every time it runs out. Gold and glowing = on.
[*][b]Hourglass - plan it once.[/b] Short of Influence? Click the hourglass beside the price and the action starts at the beginning of the first turn you can pay for it - just once, nothing is repeated. It works on independent powers too, so you can plan befriending one before you have the Influence for it.
[*][b]Either one or the other[/b] - switching one on switches the other off for that action.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]What else you get[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Only where it makes sense[/b] - the hourglass appears only when Influence is the one thing missing: not on an action you already have running, not where you must still pick a target, never on war. The sync button is locked on actions you cannot take with that leader at all right now.
[*][b]Plays by the game's limits[/b] - treaties can run with every leader; endeavours, espionage and sanctions only with as many at once as the game allows (Benjamin Franklin gets an extra endeavour). A full limit locks the sync button and its tooltip names the leader it runs with; [b]Shift+click[/b] moves it to the leader you are talking to.
[*][b]A cleaner action list[/b] - Influence prices drawn as chips in the same style as Better City UI: gold when you can start the action, greyed when you cannot, with the reason in the price's tooltip. Free actions show no price at all.
[*][b]You always know what happened[/b] - at the start of your turn a short summary lists what was proposed or started, grouped by leader with their portrait: [b]green[/b] agreed, [b]red[/b] refused, [b]grey[/b] no answer yet, [b]blue[/b] started without asking anyone (espionage, independent powers). Hover it to keep it on screen.
[*][b]Saved with your game[/b] - load an older save and you get exactly the choices it had.
[/list]

Nothing happens until you switch it on: a fresh install changes nothing.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

UI only: [b]no rules, values or balance change[/b]. Your choices are stored in the save.

[hr][/hr]
